// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 06-arithmetic
// facility: rule.arith.checked [Arith-Checked-Overflow] (u128 at its true maximum)
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.arith-overflow (dynamic)
//
// Checked addition at u128's real maximum, 2^128-1, faults. The write
// `big += 1` ends the literal binding, so the fault is found at run time
// (a literal-bound `big + 1` is refuted statically; see
// 14-control-flow/flow_literal_bound_local_overflow_static.cb).

fn main()
{
    u128 big = 340282366920938463463374607431768211454;
    big += 1;
    u128 more = big + 1;
}
